                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A small point-and-click Indie game from 2013 with an Afro-Caribbean setting.\r\n\r\nThe story is ok and the game mechanics are fine as well. The art style stands out the most and is quite unique. Their inspiration from African heritage stands out quite well. The background Jazz score accompanies the game excellently and meshes well with the overall theme. The character animations and cut scenes are done well. \r\n\r\nAs with any game of this genre, you will end up navigating the same places quite a lot of time, but that's a feature of this genre. The conversations with the NPCs provide quite the set of clues and it's good to pay attention to them.\r\n\r\nThe puzzle solving element is good and is a bit varied too. There seems to be scope of achievements in terms of trying out certain combinations - but we still have trading cards. \r\n\r\nIf I do have a gripe, it's just that getting all the free card drops in a single play might not be feasible. Otherwise, it's a fun way to spend your weekend. I do recommend getting and playing the other 2 parts for this game.\r\n\r\n- 7/10",
